 note, we record the proof of a theorem about the coincidence of genuine and homotopy fixed points for isometric group actions on complete Riemannian manifolds with nonpositive sectional curvature, and more generally, certain quotients of universal spaces for families. The result is put into context with the Nielsen realisation problem for aspherical manifolds, and we give a unifying account of different formulations of that problem, made possible by the same methods.\n\nView\n\nShow abstract\n\n... The classical Nielsen realization problem for surfaces Σ g was solved by Kerckhoff [Ker83] for all finite subgroups G ≤ Mod(Σ g ); the special case of finite cyclic subgroups G was solved earlier by Nielsen [Nie43] and Fenchel [Fen48]. In higher dimensions, Raymond-Scott [RS77] showed that the Nielsen realization problem fails in every dimension d ≥ 3 in certain nilmanifolds. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBorel actions in nonpositively curved geometry and the Nielsen realisation problem | Article Information | J-GLOBAL (https://jglobal.jst.go.jp/en/detail?JGLOBAL_ID=202502209959375111)\nciteturn2search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: last year; Crawled: 5 months ago; # Borel actions in nonpositively curved geometry and the Nielsen realisation problem ... arXiv\n\n# Borel actions in nonpositively curved geometry and the Nielsen realisation problem\n\nAuthor (1)：\n\nKremer Christian\n\nAbout Kremer Christian\n\n  * Search \"202650001248377863\"\n  * Search \"Kremer Christian\"\n\nMaterial：\n\narXiv\n\nAbout arXiv\n\n  * Search \"O7000B\"\n\nPublication year： Oct. 24, 2025  update date on preprint server： Oct. 27, 2025\nJST Material Number： O7000B  Document type： Preprint\nArticle type： プレプリント  Language： ENGLISH (EN)\n\nAbstract/Point：\n\nAbstract/Point\nJapanese summary of the article(about several hundred characters).\nAll summary is available on JDreamIII(charged).\nOn J-GLOBAL, this item will be available after more than